# st commands that only make sense on the workstation. On an agent host the
# st guard refuses them at once instead of acting on the wrong machine or
# waiting on a service that is not forwarded. One command per line, then the
# reason. "command:subcommand" names one subcommand and wins over its command;
# "allow" instead of a reason re-allows that subcommand.
snap         Btrfs snapshots of workstation projects
snaps        Btrfs snapshots of workstation projects
recover      Btrfs snapshots of workstation projects
rollback     Btrfs snapshots of workstation projects
prune        Btrfs snapshots of workstation projects
abandon      rolls back through workstation snapshots
backup       workstation backups
service      builds and restarts workstation services
runtime      workstation service runtime
logs         workstation service journals
monitor      workstation host monitor
docker       workstation Docker stacks
setup        workstation host setup
vm           Proxmox control runs from the workstation
db           the SummitFlow database is not forwarded
cleanup      workstation workspace residue
checkpoints  workstation checkpoint artifacts
elevate      owner taps run on the workstation
browser      managed browsers run on the workstation lab
ui           the desktop is on the workstation
selection    the desktop is on the workstation
show         shows files to the owner through the workstation's Tether
tether       this host's Tether is reached through the workstation hub
aico         Aico runs on the workstation; create remote agents with --host there
aico:wake    allow
wiki         the Vault lives on the workstation
bugout       lab runs from the workstation
bugout-deployment lab runs from the workstation
ominull      production observation runs from the workstation
ominull-backup production backups run from the workstation
neri         Neri state and case data stay on the workstation
